{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he shall speak for you.</b> On your behalf he shall speak to the people. And this proves regarding every לְךָ and לִי and לוֹ and לָכֶם and לָהֶם adjacent to דִּבּוּר — that all of them are in the sense of 'on behalf of them.'" "<b>He shall be to you for a mouth.</b> For an interpreter — because you are heavy of mouth." "<b>For Elohim.</b> For a master and for a minister."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:47.468710651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}